  "result": "I fixed it. In `--help`, each option's flags were listed long form first (`--name, -n`) instead of the usual short form first (`-n, --name`).\n\n**Cause:** `join_options` in `src/click/formatting.py:319` builds the flag list for each option. It sorts the flags by prefix length, but with `reverse=True`, so `--` flags came before `-` flags.\n\n**Fix:** I removed `reverse=True`. Because the sort is stable, flags with the same prefix length keep the order they were declared in.\n\nBefore and after:\n```\n--name, -n TEXT              \u2192  -n, --name TEXT\n--verbose, -v / --quiet, -q  \u2192  -v, --verbose / -q, --quiet\n```\n\nThe full test suite passes: 1906 passed, 102 skipped. I haven't committed the change.",
